{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1794436852","published":"2026-11-11T22:41:07Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:28:33.940978076Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-123863","CVE-2026-123864","CVE-2026-123865","CVE-2026-123866","CVE-2026-48937"],"summary":"nodejs: Fix of 4 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-123863: release the header fields a reset HTTP/2 stream had\n  already accepted when the stream is removed from its session, so a stream\n  that outlives its session can no longer abort the process in\n  ~Http2Session()\n- CVE-2026-123864: skip the TLS read on an empty write issued while a TLS\n  cycle is running and reject HTTP parser data callbacks that point outside\n  the buffer being executed, so a nested llhttp_execute() can no longer copy\n  server heap memory into an HTTPS request body\n- CVE-2026-123865, CVE-2026-48937: tear down an HTTP/2 session when nghttp2\n  terminates it internally after a protocol error, also while a graceful\n  close started by a peer GOAWAY is in progress, so the socket and the\n  session state are no longer held forever\n- CVE-2026-123866: keep every queued HTTP/2 write alive until the socket\n  write that carries its data completes, so a stream torn down during a\n  backpressured write can no longer send freed memory to the peer","affected":[{"package":{"name":"nodejs","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.2","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/nodejs?distro=almalinux-9.2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:16.20.2-8.el9_2.tuxcare.els29"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.2esu/CLSA-2026-1794436852.json"}},{"package":{"name":"nodejs-devel","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.2","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/nodejs-devel?distro=almalinux-9.2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:16.20.2-8.el9_2.tuxcare.els29"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.2esu/CLSA-